 cite for jaywalking and one of  the tools we had in regards to  jaywalking is it's not for us to do that  it's more for education and the  education standpoint is you educate the  pedestrian and not jaywalk  but it's a horrific situation for the  normal citizen that's driving down the  street minding their business driving  safely  that pedestrian jumps out and they're  involved in a fatal accident that  affects  that person in their vehicle also not  only the pedestrian that was killed  but the person who's driving that  affects your entire life it could  because you've killed somebody in an  accident  that wasn't your fault it is an ongoing  issue assistant sheriff brett zimmerman  we do appreciate you joining us this  morning  if you at home have a question for metro  police submit it at eight newsnow dot  com you can find out if your question is  answered every wednesday
 

